# Line endings are content, not formatting, for the knowledge corpus.
#
# `core.autocrlf=true` (the Windows default) checks Markdown out as CRLF. The
# knowledge chunker splits paragraphs on two consecutive `\n`, which CRLF text
# never contains — so a CRLF checkout silently degrades every embedding built
# from `docs/`, and only on Windows. Pinning the working tree to LF makes the
# corpus byte-identical on every machine and in CI.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets: never touched.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.mp3 binary
*.mp4 binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
